1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,869
In October 2020, two men came up from San

2
00:00:03,869 --> 00:00:07,507
Diego to Lomita, a small city in Los Angeles County.

3
00:00:08,007 --> 00:00:09,419
They had been lured there.

4
00:00:09,419 --> 00:00:10,887
Both were shot in the head.

5
00:00:11,887 --> 00:00:14,105
Federal prosecutors say the order for that

6
00:00:14,105 --> 00:00:16,324
double murder didn't come from the street.

7
00:00:16,724 --> 00:00:19,324
It came from a man serving time inside a

8
00:00:19,324 --> 00:00:20,884
California state prison.

9
00:00:21,984 --> 00:00:25,013
In August, a federal court convicted the gunman.

10
00:00:25,013 --> 00:00:27,790
On Monday, November 23, he's scheduled to be

11
00:00:27,790 --> 00:00:28,421
sentenced.

12
00:00:28,421 --> 00:00:31,008
The law gives the judge one option. Life.

13
00:00:32,008 --> 00:00:34,651
The gang behind that order has run violence

14
00:00:34,651 --> 00:00:36,924
from behind prison walls for decades.

15
00:00:36,924 --> 00:00:38,707
Lately, with smuggled phones.

16
00:00:39,407 --> 00:00:41,925
And one of the biggest recent federal cases

17
00:00:41,925 --> 00:00:44,268
against its leaders turned on one thing.

18
00:00:44,268 --> 00:00:46,319
The DEA, listening to their phones.

19
00:00:46,819 --> 00:00:49,208
Phones they were never supposed to have.

20
00:00:50,508 --> 00:00:52,577
Case file 021.

21
00:00:54,977 --> 00:00:57,413
The Aryan Brotherhood was born inside

22
00:00:57,413 --> 00:00:58,796
California's prisons.

23
00:00:59,296 --> 00:01:02,140
Federal prosecutors in California say it was

24
00:01:02,140 --> 00:01:04,855
formed in about 1964, by white inmates who

25
00:01:04,855 --> 00:01:07,893
wanted power and authority inside prison walls.

26
00:01:08,493 --> 00:01:10,968
Most accounts put its start at San Quentin.

27
00:01:11,468 --> 00:01:13,281
Members call it the Brand.

28
00:01:14,081 --> 00:01:16,289
One of its leaders, caught on a federal

29
00:01:16,289 --> 00:01:18,667
wiretap, summed up the code in four words.

30
00:01:18,667 --> 00:01:19,799
Blood in, blood out.

31
00:01:19,799 --> 00:01:22,346
Meaning, prosecutors said, you had to kill to

32
00:01:22,346 --> 00:01:22,743
get in.

33
00:01:23,843 --> 00:01:26,637
The government has gone after this gang before.

34
00:01:27,037 --> 00:01:29,818
In 2002, federal prosecutors in Los Angeles

35
00:01:29,818 --> 00:01:32,728
indicted forty alleged members and associates

36
00:01:32,728 --> 00:01:35,379
under the racketeering law known as RICO.

37
00:01:35,979 --> 00:01:38,890
The indictment was more than a hundred pages long.

38
00:01:38,890 --> 00:01:41,044
It accused the gang of 32 murders and

39
00:01:41,044 --> 00:01:43,664
attempted murders, going back decades, and up

40
00:01:43,664 --> 00:01:46,517
to 16 defendants faced a possible death sentence.

41
00:01:47,117 --> 00:01:50,104
19 defendants took plea deals before trial.

42
00:01:50,604 --> 00:01:54,017
The leaders went on trial in Santa Ana in 2006.

43
00:01:54,517 --> 00:01:56,816
Two of them, Barry Mills and Tyler Bingham,

44
00:01:56,816 --> 00:01:59,061
were convicted of racketeering and murder.

45
00:01:59,661 --> 00:02:01,351
Mills was known as the Baron.

46
00:02:01,351 --> 00:02:02,574
Bingham, as the Hulk.

47
00:02:02,574 --> 00:02:05,196
Two more members were convicted of conspiring

48
00:02:05,196 --> 00:02:06,595
to murder Black inmates.

49
00:02:07,195 --> 00:02:09,580
Prosecutors asked for the death penalty.

50
00:02:09,580 --> 00:02:10,773
The jury deadlocked.

51
00:02:10,773 --> 00:02:12,741
Both men got life without parole.

52
00:02:13,641 --> 00:02:16,163
For Mills, the vote was 9–3 for death.

53
00:02:16,163 --> 00:02:17,093
Not unanimous.

54
00:02:17,093 --> 00:02:18,553
So the judge, David O.

55
00:02:18,553 --> 00:02:21,407
Carter, declared a mistrial on the penalty.

56
00:02:22,207 --> 00:02:25,367
Mills died in his cell at the federal supermax

57
00:02:25,367 --> 00:02:27,497
in Florence, Colorado, in 2018.

58
00:02:28,197 --> 00:02:30,475
But putting the leaders in the most secure

59
00:02:30,475 --> 00:02:32,699
prison in America didn't end the Brand in

60
00:02:32,699 --> 00:02:33,296
California.

61
00:02:33,896 --> 00:02:36,589
Because by then, the gang had found a new tool.

62
00:02:36,589 --> 00:02:37,907
And it fit in a pocket.

63
00:02:39,107 --> 00:02:41,747
A cell phone inside a prison is contraband.

64
00:02:41,747 --> 00:02:43,651
It's also worth a lot of money.

65
00:02:44,251 --> 00:02:47,208
In 2009, California's Inspector General

66
00:02:47,208 --> 00:02:50,317
reported that inmates were paying $500 to

67
00:02:50,317 --> 00:02:51,909
$1,000 for one phone.

68
00:02:52,509 --> 00:02:56,963
That same report counted the phones seized by

69
00:02:56,963 --> 00:03:01,021
the prison system. 261 in 2006. Then 992.

70
00:03:01,021 --> 00:03:02,109
Then 2,811.

71
00:03:02,809 --> 00:03:05,714
A decade later, the numbers were in a

72
00:03:05,714 --> 00:03:07,048
different league.

73
00:03:07,048 --> 00:03:10,895
In 2019 alone, the department confiscated 10,494.

74
00:03:11,895 --> 00:03:15,678
Then 9,209 in 2020.

75
00:03:15,678 --> 00:03:18,465
8,452 in 2021.

76
00:03:19,065 --> 00:03:21,514
The state has tried dogs, searches, and a

77
00:03:21,514 --> 00:03:23,963
managed access system built to detect and

78
00:03:23,963 --> 00:03:24,740
block phones.

79
00:03:24,740 --> 00:03:25,935
They keep coming in.

80
00:03:26,735 --> 00:03:29,561
Dogs alone found more than 2,000 phones in

81
00:03:29,561 --> 00:03:31,983
2019, by the department's own count.

82
00:03:32,583 --> 00:03:35,228
Back in 2009, the Inspector General reported

83
00:03:35,228 --> 00:03:37,753
that the department's own officials called

84
00:03:37,753 --> 00:03:40,098
cell phones one of the most significant

85
00:03:40,098 --> 00:03:41,180
problems it faced.

86
00:03:42,180 --> 00:03:45,209
For a prison gang, a phone changes everything.

87
00:03:45,709 --> 00:03:48,125
A note smuggled out of a cell can take days.

88
00:03:48,125 --> 00:03:49,278
A call takes seconds.

89
00:03:49,278 --> 00:03:51,748
A text can reach a member three prisons away,

90
00:03:51,748 --> 00:03:54,328
or a dealer on the street, or a man with a gun.

91
00:03:55,028 --> 00:03:57,334
By the 2010s, the Aryan Brotherhood had a

92
00:03:57,334 --> 00:03:59,865
leadership commission of three men, according

93
00:03:59,865 --> 00:04:01,833
to prosecutors and court reporting.

94
00:04:02,333 --> 00:04:04,662
The Justice Department says Troxell rose to

95
00:04:04,662 --> 00:04:06,829
that commission in the early 2000s, when

96
00:04:06,829 --> 00:04:09,104
nearly all of the gang's prominent members

97
00:04:09,104 --> 00:04:11,108
were held at Pelican Bay, the state's

98
00:04:11,108 --> 00:04:13,491
high-security prison near the Oregon border.

99
00:04:14,091 --> 00:04:16,551
Two of them were serving life sentences in

100
00:04:16,551 --> 00:04:17,664
California prisons.

101
00:04:17,664 --> 00:04:20,182
And both, the DEA would later show, were on

102
00:04:20,182 --> 00:04:20,768
the phone.

103
00:04:21,668 --> 00:04:23,503
One was Danny Troxell.

104
00:04:24,003 --> 00:04:26,712
The other was the man at the center of this

105
00:04:26,712 --> 00:04:27,342
case file.

106
00:04:27,342 --> 00:04:28,287
Ronald Yandell.

107
00:04:28,287 --> 00:04:30,744
The AP reported his nickname. Renegade.

108
00:04:31,744 --> 00:04:33,949
When the federal case against him began,

109
00:04:33,949 --> 00:04:36,209
Ronald Yandell was already serving a life

110
00:04:36,209 --> 00:04:37,312
sentence for murder.

111
00:04:37,912 --> 00:04:41,432
CBS News reported it as 65 years to life.

112
00:04:41,932 --> 00:04:43,365
He wasn't going anywhere.

113
00:04:43,365 --> 00:04:45,659
And according to federal prosecutors, he

114
00:04:45,659 --> 00:04:46,519
didn't need to.

115
00:04:47,519 --> 00:04:49,929
Yandell shared a cell with another member,

116
00:04:49,929 --> 00:04:50,847
Billy Sylvester.

117
00:04:51,347 --> 00:04:53,862
And from that shared cell, prosecutors said,

118
00:04:53,862 --> 00:04:56,377
the two of them ran a significant heroin and

119
00:04:56,377 --> 00:04:58,892
methamphetamine trafficking operation, using

120
00:04:58,892 --> 00:05:00,264
smuggled-in cell phones.

121
00:05:01,164 --> 00:05:03,752
The network, according to the charges, reached

122
00:05:03,752 --> 00:05:06,340
Sacramento, Southern California, Missouri, and

123
00:05:06,340 --> 00:05:06,903
Las Vegas.

124
00:05:07,503 --> 00:05:09,296
And the Brand didn't work alone.

125
00:05:09,296 --> 00:05:11,706
The charges said Yandell and another member

126
00:05:11,706 --> 00:05:14,004
had a drug partnership with an inmate the

127
00:05:14,004 --> 00:05:16,190
government described as a member of the

128
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:16,975
Mexican Mafia.

129
00:05:17,675 --> 00:05:20,673
Two prison gangs that are supposed to be enemies.

130
00:05:20,673 --> 00:05:23,733
In business, according to prosecutors, over drugs.

131
00:05:24,733 --> 00:05:27,350
On the outside, the network needed people with

132
00:05:27,350 --> 00:05:28,147
clean records.

133
00:05:28,647 --> 00:05:31,117
One of them was a 70-year-old woman from

134
00:05:31,117 --> 00:05:33,154
Calimesa, in Southern California.

135
00:05:33,154 --> 00:05:35,871
Kathleen Nolan pleaded guilty to her part in

136
00:05:35,871 --> 00:05:38,341
the drug trafficking conspiracy, and was

137
00:05:38,341 --> 00:05:39,761
sentenced to 36 months.

138
00:05:40,561 --> 00:05:41,859
Drugs moved in, too.

139
00:05:41,859 --> 00:05:43,676
Into the prisons themselves.

140
00:05:44,176 --> 00:05:47,020
The 2019 charges described phones and drugs

141
00:05:47,020 --> 00:05:49,930
hidden in food packages mailed to inmates at

142
00:05:49,930 --> 00:05:51,451
Folsom and High Desert.

143
00:05:51,951 --> 00:05:54,527
And an attempt, in August 2016, to carry

144
00:05:54,527 --> 00:05:57,168
methamphetamine, phones, and tobacco into

145
00:05:57,168 --> 00:05:58,585
Folsom during a visit.

146
00:05:59,285 --> 00:06:01,991
The man accused in that visit was a lawyer.

147
00:06:01,991 --> 00:06:04,633
His case was dismissed in 2025, reportedly

148
00:06:04,633 --> 00:06:06,521
because he was terminally ill.

149
00:06:06,521 --> 00:06:07,968
He was never convicted.

150
00:06:08,868 --> 00:06:09,875
Drugs meant money.

151
00:06:09,875 --> 00:06:12,394
And in this gang, money and violence were the

152
00:06:12,394 --> 00:06:13,177
same business.

153
00:06:13,777 --> 00:06:16,615
At trial, a federal prosecutor put it plainly.

154
00:06:17,015 --> 00:06:19,694
The violence, the murders, is what gave these

155
00:06:19,694 --> 00:06:22,433
defendants power as Aryan Brotherhood members.

156
00:06:23,533 --> 00:06:26,080
The charges listed killing after killing

157
00:06:26,080 --> 00:06:27,736
inside California prisons.

158
00:06:28,336 --> 00:06:30,750
October 2011, at Folsom State Prison.

159
00:06:30,750 --> 00:06:32,120
An inmate was killed.

160
00:06:32,120 --> 00:06:35,056
Sylvester was later convicted of that murder.

161
00:06:35,656 --> 00:06:36,519
October 2016.

162
00:06:36,519 --> 00:06:39,442
An inmate killed at High Desert State Prison

163
00:06:39,442 --> 00:06:40,372
in Susanville.

164
00:06:40,372 --> 00:06:42,099
Another at Salinas Valley.

165
00:06:42,599 --> 00:06:45,128
The man charged with the Salinas Valley

166
00:06:45,128 --> 00:06:47,981
killing, Brant Daniel, was sentenced to life

167
00:06:47,981 --> 00:06:49,084
in December 2023.

168
00:06:49,684 --> 00:06:50,511
July 2018.

169
00:06:50,511 --> 00:06:53,076
Another killing at High Desert.

170
00:06:53,676 --> 00:06:55,704
Two members later admitted that one.

171
00:06:55,704 --> 00:06:57,676
The victim, according to their plea

172
00:06:57,676 --> 00:07:00,155
agreements, had falsely claimed to be in the

173
00:07:00,155 --> 00:07:03,084
Aryan Brotherhood, and had run up a large drug debt.

174
00:07:03,784 --> 00:07:06,395
One of them said he did it to keep his status

175
00:07:06,395 --> 00:07:07,091
in the gang.

176
00:07:08,191 --> 00:07:10,623
And then there was August 2015.

177
00:07:11,423 --> 00:07:14,435
On the grounds of the Folsom prison complex, a

178
00:07:14,435 --> 00:07:16,399
71-year-old inmate was killed.

179
00:07:16,399 --> 00:07:18,953
He was a leader of a rival prison gang.

180
00:07:19,553 --> 00:07:21,183
His death set off a riot.

181
00:07:21,183 --> 00:07:24,051
The AP reported that 11 prisoners were taken

182
00:07:24,051 --> 00:07:25,420
to outside hospitals.

183
00:07:26,320 --> 00:07:28,979
Court records described him as a high-value

184
00:07:28,979 --> 00:07:30,587
target for the enterprise.

185
00:07:31,587 --> 00:07:32,736
Who wanted him dead?

186
00:07:32,736 --> 00:07:34,979
For a while, that was a prison mystery.

187
00:07:35,779 --> 00:07:38,375
Then, about a year later, Yandell picked up

188
00:07:38,375 --> 00:07:38,979
his phone.

189
00:07:40,279 --> 00:07:43,305
In 2016, the Drug Enforcement Administration

190
00:07:43,305 --> 00:07:44,268
was listening.

191
00:07:44,968 --> 00:07:47,372
The case was a drug investigation first.

192
00:07:47,372 --> 00:07:49,895
The DEA led it, with the California prison

193
00:07:49,895 --> 00:07:52,179
system and local and federal partners.

194
00:07:52,679 --> 00:07:54,972
Court-authorized wiretaps went up on

195
00:07:54,972 --> 00:07:57,329
contraband phones inside the prisons.

196
00:07:57,929 --> 00:08:00,169
And the men on those phones talked.

197
00:08:01,169 --> 00:08:03,896
According to the Justice Department, about a

198
00:08:03,896 --> 00:08:06,127
year after the 2015 killing, the DEA

199
00:08:06,127 --> 00:08:08,978
intercepted calls Yandell made on a contraband

200
00:08:08,978 --> 00:08:09,660
cell phone.

201
00:08:10,260 --> 00:08:12,464
On those calls, the department says, he

202
00:08:12,464 --> 00:08:14,441
bragged about directing the murder.

203
00:08:15,241 --> 00:08:17,181
And about sponsoring the killers for

204
00:08:17,181 --> 00:08:18,420
membership in the gang.

205
00:08:19,620 --> 00:08:21,433
It wasn't only Yandell.

206
00:08:21,833 --> 00:08:24,181
The same wiretaps, the Justice Department

207
00:08:24,181 --> 00:08:26,701
says, captured Danny Troxell discussing gang

208
00:08:26,701 --> 00:08:28,361
business with another member.

209
00:08:28,861 --> 00:08:31,134
And ordering the murder of another Aryan

210
00:08:31,134 --> 00:08:33,236
Brotherhood member, who was housed at

211
00:08:33,236 --> 00:08:34,600
Calipatria State Prison.

212
00:08:35,500 --> 00:08:38,349
Jurors would later hear hours of those recordings.

213
00:08:38,349 --> 00:08:40,971
The Mercury News reported that on one of them,

214
00:08:40,971 --> 00:08:43,820
Yandell described how to kill with a prison knife.

215
00:08:44,620 --> 00:08:46,369
Think about what that means.

216
00:08:46,869 --> 00:08:49,363
The phones were the gang's greatest weapon.

217
00:08:49,363 --> 00:08:51,973
They let a man serving life in one prison run

218
00:08:51,973 --> 00:08:54,293
drugs and order violence across a state.

219
00:08:54,893 --> 00:08:57,147
And the same phones were recording the

220
00:08:57,147 --> 00:08:58,392
evidence against him.

221
00:08:59,692 --> 00:09:03,575
On June 6, 2019, the Justice Department went public.

222
00:09:04,175 --> 00:09:06,591
16 members and associates of the Aryan

223
00:09:06,591 --> 00:09:08,180
Brotherhood were charged.

224
00:09:08,180 --> 00:09:10,660
Racketeering, murder, drug trafficking.

225
00:09:11,460 --> 00:09:14,609
Nine of them were already inside California prisons.

226
00:09:14,609 --> 00:09:17,092
Six were already serving life for murder.

227
00:09:17,692 --> 00:09:20,073
The rest were arrested on the outside, or had

228
00:09:20,073 --> 00:09:21,237
warrants out for them.

229
00:09:21,237 --> 00:09:23,618
Among them, the charges said, were people who

230
00:09:23,618 --> 00:09:25,628
handled the money and moved the drugs.

231
00:09:26,228 --> 00:09:28,829
The government's case accused the gang of five

232
00:09:28,829 --> 00:09:31,092
murders inside prisons, and several more

233
00:09:31,092 --> 00:09:32,223
murder conspiracies.

234
00:09:33,023 --> 00:09:35,400
And for a while, the release warned, several

235
00:09:35,400 --> 00:09:37,993
defendants could face the federal death penalty.

236
00:09:38,593 --> 00:09:41,296
California's corrections secretary at the time

237
00:09:41,296 --> 00:09:43,647
said neutralizing prison gangs was a top

238
00:09:43,647 --> 00:09:45,292
priority for his department.

239
00:09:46,092 --> 00:09:46,601
The U.S.

240
00:09:46,601 --> 00:09:49,528
Attorney in Sacramento, McGregor Scott, called

241
00:09:49,528 --> 00:09:51,882
the charges a significant blow to the

242
00:09:51,882 --> 00:09:54,617
leadership of a violent criminal enterprise

243
00:09:54,617 --> 00:09:56,844
run from inside California prisons.

244
00:09:57,744 --> 00:09:59,899
Then came years of legal fights.

245
00:10:00,299 --> 00:10:02,971
In December 2022, a superseding indictment

246
00:10:02,971 --> 00:10:05,325
added murder charges against Yandell,

247
00:10:05,325 --> 00:10:07,552
Sylvester, and three other members.

248
00:10:08,152 --> 00:10:08,870
The next U.S.

249
00:10:08,870 --> 00:10:11,023
Attorney, Phillip Talbert, said the new

250
00:10:11,023 --> 00:10:13,397
indictment struck at the heart of the Aryan

251
00:10:13,397 --> 00:10:14,723
Brotherhood prison gang.

252
00:10:15,423 --> 00:10:18,133
In October 2023, prosecutors filed a notice

253
00:10:18,133 --> 00:10:19,078
with the court.

254
00:10:19,078 --> 00:10:22,292
They would not seek the death penalty in this case.

255
00:10:23,192 --> 00:10:25,655
By the time the trial came, some defendants

256
00:10:25,655 --> 00:10:26,743
had pleaded guilty.

257
00:10:26,743 --> 00:10:28,461
Others were already sentenced.

258
00:10:29,061 --> 00:10:31,171
Three were left to face a jury.

259
00:10:31,171 --> 00:10:33,349
Yandell, Sylvester, and Troxell.

260
00:10:34,349 --> 00:10:37,740
The trial opened in Sacramento on February 26,

261
00:10:37,740 --> 00:10:39,436
2024, before Chief U.S.

262
00:10:39,436 --> 00:10:41,795
District Judge Kimberly Mueller.

263
00:10:42,395 --> 00:10:44,144
It lasted nine weeks.

264
00:10:44,644 --> 00:10:47,537
Of the 16 people charged in 2019, several took

265
00:10:47,537 --> 00:10:48,229
plea deals.

266
00:10:48,229 --> 00:10:50,744
One, who was never arrested, had died by

267
00:10:50,744 --> 00:10:53,889
suicide in Costa Rica, Prison Legal News reported.

268
00:10:53,889 --> 00:10:56,719
And the man charged as a Mexican Mafia member

269
00:10:56,719 --> 00:10:59,360
was stabbed to death by other prisoners in

270
00:10:59,360 --> 00:11:01,561
2023, before he ever went to trial.

271
00:11:02,361 --> 00:11:05,021
The prosecutor told jurors that every Aryan

272
00:11:05,021 --> 00:11:07,865
Brotherhood murder sends a terrifying message.

273
